# CONSULT-54 (Cursor) — File:line findings

## Task 1 — Geometric case in `FreeChaseCamera::alter`

### Transform chain (pivot placement)

```630:677:D:\Code\swg-client-v2\src\engine\client\library\clientGame\src\shared\camera\FreeChaseCamera.cpp
	//-- move camera to the avatar's cell and position
	{
		const CellProperty* const targetCell = m_target->getParentCell ();
		if (getParentCell () != targetCell)
			setParentCell (const_cast<CellProperty*> (targetCell));
		// ...
		setTransform_o2p (targetObject->getTransform_o2c ());
		// ...
		yaw_o (m_yaw_w + (ms_cameraMode == CM_chase ? m_offsetYaw_w : 0.f));
		m_offset = Vector::linearInterpolate(m_offset, m_desiredOffset, elapsedTime);
		move_o(Vector(m_offset.x, m_offset.y + ms_vehicleCameraOffsetY, m_offset.z));
		pitch_o (ms_pitch);
	}
```

- **Pivot** = `getPosition_w()` after this block: avatar cell origin + shoulder/height offset, with camera yaw/pitch applied.
- **Camera parent cell** is forced to the **player’s cell** (632–634). It is **never** updated to wherever the zoomed-out camera actually ends up.

### Shoulder side-ray (above collision block)

```683:699:D:\Code\swg-client-v2\src\engine\client\library\clientGame\src\shared\camera\FreeChaseCamera.cpp
	// prevent shoulder cam from clipping geometry (due to near plane)
	if (creatureObject && m_currentZoom >= scaledFirstPersonDistance)
	{
		CollisionInfo result;
		Vector startPos_w = creatureObject->getPosition_w();
		startPos_w.y += m_desiredOffset.y;
		Vector endPos_w = startPos_w + (creatureObject->rotate_o2w(Vector::unitX) * (m_desiredOffset.x + 0.25f));
		if(ClientWorld::collide(getParentCell(),startPos_w,endPos_w,...))
		{
			m_offset.x = linearInterpolate (m_offset.x, 0.0f, clamp (0.f, elapsedTime * cs_cameraPullInSpeed, 1.f));
		}
	}
```

This ray is **avatar-frame +X**, not camera-frame. It only eases shoulder offset; it does **not** constrain backward zoom.

### Main collision block (diamond default)

```711:792:D:\Code\swg-client-v2\src\engine\client\library\clientGame\src\shared\camera\FreeChaseCamera.cpp
		const Vector cameraZ_p = Vector::negativeUnitZ * m_zoom;   // desired zoom, NOT m_currentZoom
		const Vector start_w   = getPosition_w ();                  // pivot
		const Vector end_w     = start_w + rotate_o2w (cameraZ_p); // desired camera endpoint

		// 4 rays: pivot±0.25 in camera-local ±X/±Y → same endpoint offset
		// ...
		if (hit)
			m_currentZoom = Lerp(start_w, end_w, minimumT).distance(start_w);
		// ...
		move_o (Vector::negativeUnitZ * m_currentZoom);  // actual placement
```

### Concrete geometry: “near wall, look away from wall”

Assume player stands close to interior wall **W**, camera yaw rotated so view direction **V** points **away from W** (into the room).

| Element | Location |
|---|---|
| **Pivot** (`start_w`) | ~0.5–1.5 m inside the cell, near W (player + `m_offset`) |
| **Desired endpoint** (`end_w`) | `start_w + rotate_o2w(-Z * m_zoom)` — **behind the view axis**, i.e. opposite **V**, which points **toward W** |
| **Actual camera** | Pivot + `rotate_o2w(-Z * m_currentZoom)` via `move_o` at line 792 |

The 4 diamond rays (728–763) are parallel to the main segment, each offset ±0.25 m in camera-local X/Y. They test a **0.5 m cross-section tube** from pivot to desired endpoint. They do **not** test from the final camera position back toward the pivot.

All queries use `getParentCell()` = **player’s interior cell** (718/752). In a non-world cell, `ClientWorld::internalCollide` hits only the **cell owner structure** plus portal recursion:

```1609:1641:D:\Code\client-tools\src\engine\client\library\clientGame\src\shared\core\ClientWorld.cpp
	else
	{
		Object const & object = cellProperty->getOwner ();
		if (internalCollideObject (flags, &object, startPosition_w, result.getPoint (), ...))
			{ collided = true; result = info; }
	}
	// portal crossing recurses into destinationCellProperty at truncated t
```

### Why wall W might not stop the camera — ranked

| Mechanism | Likelihood | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| **A. Ray miss → no `m_colliding` → full zoom placement** | **Highest for “on far side”** | 741–742, 766–771, 792 |
| **B. Camera extruded outside cell; render uses player cell for DPVS** | **High for visual see-through** (may not require true geometric pass-through) | 632–634, 872–889 `RenderWorld.cpp` |
| **C. OUR rate-limit + recovery fight leaves camera outside despite hits** | **High in OUR only** (REFERENCE snaps instantly) | OUR 620–628, 774–786 vs REF 602, 666–667, 746 |
| **D. Diamond path lacks 0.25 m near-plane pullback** | Low–medium (penetration, not full pass-through) | Diamond 754 vs simple 721 |
| **E. `CF_interiorGeometry` is a no-op** | Explains data-dependent misses, not tree delta | Flag defined `ClientWorld.h:47,59`; **never read** in `ClientWorld.cpp` |
| **F. Wrong cell for query** | Unlikely as primary cause | Cell is player cell; portal recursion handles crossings |
| **G. Back-face / one-sided mesh** | Possible data issue | Inside `appearance->collide()` via `internalCollideObjectTest` |

**Most likely miss path for “camera on far side”:** **A** — the segment `start_w → end_w` does not register a hit on the structure owner mesh (missing/thin collidable shell, portal traversal continuing the ray — `ClientWorld.cpp:1621–1641`), so `m_colliding` stays false and line 792 places the camera at full `m_currentZoom` through W.

**Most likely for the symptom as observed (see exterior through wall):** **B** — camera world position is outside the cell hull while `getParentCell()` remains the interior cell:

```872:889:D:\Code\client-tools\src\engine\client\library\clientGraphics\src\shared\RenderWorld.cpp
	ms_cameraCell = camera.getParentCell();
	ms_dpvsCameraCell = ms_cameraCell->getDpvsCell();
	ms_cameraToWorld = camera.getTransform_o2w();
	// ...
	ms_dpvsCamera->setCell(ms_dpvsCameraCell);
	ms_dpvsCamera->setCameraToCellMatrix(convertToDpvsTransform(camera.getTransform_o2c(), ...));
```

DPVS visibility is resolved from the **player cell**, not from “which cell actually contains the camera world position.” Pressing the chase camera against a back wall (large `m_currentZoom`, no interior cap) is exactly when this mismatch bites — matching the zoom-cap comment at lines 605–612.

