## Task 2 — REFERENCE extra keep-visible paths

**Result: No additional indoor wall keep-visible mechanism in REFERENCE that OUR lacks.**

### Searched and ruled out

| Area | Finding |
|---|---|
| **`FreeChaseCamera.cpp`** | Collision block byte-identical; REFERENCE has **instant** shoulder snap (666–667), no `cs_cameraPullInSpeed`, no interior zoom cap |
| **`DebugPortalCamera.cpp`** | Debug fly camera only; **no** `ClientWorld::collide` |
| **`CockpitCamera.cpp` / `FlyByCamera.cpp`** | **No** camera-wall collision |
| **`GameCamera::alter`** | Jitter/flash only; **no** wall push (`GameCamera.cpp:163–198`) |
| **`GroundScene.cpp`** | Normal play uses `CI_freeChase` (761); `ClientWorld::collide` at 2244 is **`#ifdef _DEBUG` only** |
| **`CollisionWorld.cpp`** | **No** camera-specific queries |
| **`ConfigClientGame.cpp`** | Identical defaults: `cameraNearPlane=0.25f` (972), `freeChaseCameraMaximumZoom=1.f` (1052), `freeChaseCameraZoomSpeed=0.2f` (1122) |
| **`cameraSimpleCollision`** | Default `false` (`FreeChaseCamera.cpp:960–962`); UI checkbox in `SwgCuiOptGraphics.cpp:218` only — same in both trees |
| **`CF_interiorGeometry`** | Defined in `ClientWorld.h:47,59` but **never consumed** in collide implementation |

### Only tangential camera–collision touchpoints (not keep-visible)

- `GlowAppearance.cpp:369–370` — glow occlusion test, not camera placement
- `ShipTurretCamera.cpp:191` — ship turret only
- `CelestialObject.cpp:202` — sun/moon line-of-sight

**Indoor ground chase = `FreeChaseCamera` collision + render portal cull. No hidden REFERENCE path.**

---

## Single best root-cause hypothesis

**The chase camera is placed by shared collision code that can fail to constrain position when (1) the pivot→endpoint ray misses the structure collidable shell, or (2) OUR post-collision `cs_cameraPullInSpeed` rate-limiting lets `m_currentZoom` sit beyond the wall while recovery lerp pushes outward — a delta REFERENCE avoids by instant snap. The visible “see-through” is compounded by a render-side cell mismatch: the camera’s world position exits the player cell volume while `getParentCell()` / DPVS still treat it as inside (`RenderWorld.cpp:872–889`), flipping portal visibility at back-wall zoom distances — which is why the 3 m interior zoom cap works as a band-aid without touching the collision algorithm itself.**

**Where to investigate next (not porting camera code):**
1. Runtime probe: log `getPosition_w()`, `getParentCell()`, and `PortalProperty::findContainingCell(cameraPos)` when symptom occurs — confirms B vs A.
2. Compare structure collision mesh / portal layout for the repro POB between OUR and REFERENCE game data (not source).
3. Re-evaluate OUR `cs_cameraPullInSpeed` gating (774–786) against REFERENCE instant response — OUR-only effective behavioral delta adjacent to the identical collision block.
